  "title": "Second voyage of HMS Beagle",
  "summary": "HMS Beagle left Plymouth on 27 December 1831 under Robert FitzRoy on a survey voyage meant to last two years but lasting five, with the young naturalist Charles Darwin aboard. It called at the Galápagos in 1835, crossed the Pacific to Tahiti and Sydney, and reached Falmouth on 2 October 1836.",
